    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0301" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1386.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Group to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 15, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to our letter of April 12th,
                    outlining the position of the American group as regards the currency loan, we
                    beg to enclose <pb facs="0302" n="198" xml:id="pg198"/> herewith a copy of a
                    telegram from Messrs. Morgan, Grenfell &amp; Co., transmitting a message
                    received from Peking reporting the action taken in pursuance of our telegraphic
                    instructions to Mr. F. H. McKnight, in Peking, a copy of which was transmitted
                    to you with our letter above referred to.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard Straight</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d206-a1.xml" xpointer="d206-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
